"separating the single `call` into separate `submit`, `form`, `refresh` "
"and `lookup` calls. If any users have created their own Apps, they have "
"to be updated to the new system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:3410
msgid ""
"If you upgrade from a release earlier than v6.5, please read the other "
"[Important Upgrade Notes](https://docs.mattermost.com/upgrade/important-"
"upgrade-notes.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:3415
msgid "Apps Framework 1.0: General Availability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:3416
msgid ""
"The Apps Framework allows developers to build integrations with "
"Mattermost that seamlessly work across Mattermost’s desktop and mobile "
"clients. Apps can be developed using any programming language, as opposed"
" to plugins which must be developed in Go."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:3418
msgid "Triggers and Actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:3419
msgid ""
"Channel admins can now configure [certain "
"actions](https://docs.mattermost.com/channels/create-channels.html) to be"
" executed automatically based on trigger conditions without writing any "
"code. Users running an older Playbooks release need to upgrade their "
"Playbooks instance to at least v1.26 to take advantage of the channel "
"actions functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:3421
msgid "Actions Restructure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:3422
msgid ""
"The **Actions** menu was restructured to reduce the clutter from Plugins "
"and Apps."
msgstr ""

