#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5538
msgid ""
"Release v5.32 - [Feature "
"Release](https://docs.mattermost.com/administration/release-"
"definitions.html#feature-release)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5540
msgid "**v5.32.1, released 2021-02-17**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5541
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where any search containing an underscore failed on "
"PostgreSQL databases. This was fixed by reverting a v5.32.0 feature that "
"added support for searching for terms on PostgreSQL that contain "
"underscores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5542
msgid "**v5.32.0, released 2021-02-16**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5543
msgid "Original 5.32.0 release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5545
msgid ""
"Mattermost v5.32.0 contains low level security fixes. "
"[Upgrading](https://docs.mattermost.com/administration/upgrade.html) is "
"recommended. Details will be posted on our [security updates "
"page](https://mattermost.com/security-updates/) 30 days after release as "
"per the [Mattermost Responsible Disclosure Policy](https://mattermost.com"
"/security-vulnerability-report/?redirect_source=mm-org/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5548
msgid ""
"TLS versions 1.0 and 1.1 have been deprecated by browser vendors. "
"Starting in Mattermost Server v5.32 (February 16), mmctl returns an error"
" when connected to Mattermost servers deployed with these TLS versions "
"and System Admins will need to explicitly add a flag in their commands to"
" continue to use them. We recommend upgrading to TLS version 1.2 or "
"higher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5549
msgid ""
"PostgreSQL ended long-term support for [version 9.4 in February "
"2020](https://www.postgresql.org/support/versioning). From v5.26 "
"Mattermost officially supports PostgreSQL version 10 as PostgreSQL 9.4 is"
" no longer supported. New installs will require PostgreSQL 10+. Previous "
"Mattermost versions will continue to be compatible with PostgreSQL 9.4. "
"PostgreSQL 9.4 and all 9.x versions are now fully deprecated in our v5.30"
" release (December 16, 2020). Please follow the instructions under the "
"Upgrading Section within [the PostgreSQL "
"documentation](https://www.postgresql.org/support/versioning/). "
"Mattermost will now fail to start if the Postgres version is below that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5551
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5987
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6221
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6416
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6505
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6749
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6929
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7074
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7146
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7395
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7649
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:10914
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:11418
msgid "Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5552
msgid ""
"``ExperimentalChannelOrganization``, ``EnableXToLeaveChannelsFromLHS``, "
"``CloseUnusedDirectMessages``, and ``ExperimentalHideTownSquareinLHS`` "
"settings are only functional if the Legacy Sidebar "
"(``EnableLegacySidebar``) is enabled since they are not compatible with "
"the new sidebar experience. ``ExperimentalChannelSidebarOrganization`` "
"has been deprecated, since the [new sidebar is now enabled for all "
"users](https://mattermost.com/blog/custom-collapsible-channel-"
"categories/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5553
msgid ""
"Breaking changes to the Golang client API were introduced: "
"``GetPostThread``, ``GetPostsForChannel``, ``GetPostsSince``, "
"``GetPostsAfter``, ``GetPostsBefore``, and ``GetPostsAroundLastUnread`` "
"now require an additional collapsedThreads parameter to be passed. Any "
"client making use of these functions will need to update them when "
"upgrading its dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5554
msgid ""
"[A breaking change was introduced when upgrading the Go version to "
"v1.15.5](https://go.dev/doc/go1.15) where user logins fail with AD/LDAP "
"Sync when the certificate of the LDAP Server has no Subject Alternative "
"Name (SAN) in it. Creating a new certificate on the AD/LDAP Server with "
"the SAN inside fixes this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5557
msgid ""
"If you upgrade from a release earlier than v5.31, please read the other "
"[Important Upgrade Notes](https://docs.mattermost.com/administration"
"/important-upgrade-notes.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5562
msgid "General availability of custom, collapsible channel categories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5563
msgid ""
"Mattermost now gives users flexibility to organize channels and direct "
"messages into custom, collapsible sidebar categories. Users gain full "
"personalization of their sidebar to improve productivity, reduce clutter "
"and focus on what matters. Learn more about [the new channel sidebar "
"enhancements](https://mattermost.com/blog/custom-collapsible-channel-"
"categories/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5565
msgid "Self-serve renewals (E10 & E20 Editions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5566
msgid ""
"Mattermost is introducing the ability to renew your self-managed E10 or "
"E20 license subscription online with a credit card. This feature creates "
"a frictionless experience for System Administrators to renew their "
"license without the need to contact sales."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5568
msgid "Incident Collaboration v1.3.2 (E20 Edition)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5569
msgid ""
"Pre-packaged Incident Collaboration v1.3.2 offers a more specific "
"incident status and centralized task list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5574
msgid "Added new languages, Bulgarian and Swedish."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5575
msgid "Added team sidebar user interface and animation enhancements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5576
msgid ""
"Moved the header icons to the left of the header beside the channel "
"description."
