#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5577
msgid ""
"Added support to move multi-selected groups of channels to another "
"category via the **More options** menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5580
msgid "Updated bundled plugin packages, including GitHub and Jenkins plugins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5581
msgid ""
"Enabled experimental support for ARM64 plugins by allowing any matching "
"``GOOS-GOOARCH`` combination in the plugin manifest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5584
msgid ""
"``AnalyticsPostCount`` now avoids unnecessary table scans during various "
"background jobs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5585
msgid ""
"The Help text for the Rate Limiting setting was updated to explain the "
"purpose of rate limiting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5586
msgid ""
"Removed the word \"experimental\" from the Gossip setting in the System "
"Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5587
msgid "Updated the Go version to v1.15.5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5588
msgid ""
"Added support for automatic installation and enablement of plugins using "
"feature flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5589
msgid ""
"Added ``webhook create`` endpoints to local mode and the ability to "
"create webhooks for other users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5590
msgid "Added a Mattermost CLI command to initialize the database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5591
msgid "Added support for processing import files through the API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5592
msgid "Added support for protocol-relative URLs while using the Image Proxy."
