#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5972
msgid ""
"Release v5.28 - [Feature Release](https://docs.mattermost.com/process"
"/release-faq.html#release-overview)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5974
msgid "**v5.28.2, released 2020-12-03**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5976
msgid "**v5.28.1, released 2020-10-19**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5977
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where mmctl Command Line Tool (Beta) was broken on "
"Mattermost server v5.28.0. "
"[MM-29740](https://mattermost.atlassian.net/browse/MM-29740)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5978
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6132
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6389
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where the Compliance Exports were taking too long on large"
" deployments. This was fixed with a performance optimization of the "
"message export query."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5979
msgid "**v5.28.0, released 2020-10-16**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5980
msgid "Original 5.28.0 release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5983
msgid ""
"PostgreSQL ended long-term support for [version 9.4 in February "
"2020](https://www.postgresql.org/support/versioning). Mattermost is "
"officially supporting PostgreSQL version 10 with v5.26 release as "
"PostgreSQL 9.4 is no longer supported. New installs will require "
"PostgreSQL 10+. Previous Mattermost versions, including our current ESR, "
"will continue to be compatible with PostgreSQL 9.4. We plan on fully "
"deprecating PostgreSQL 9.4 and all 9.x versions in our v5.30 release "
"(December 16, 2020). Please follow the instructions under the Upgrading "
"Section within [the PostgreSQL "
"documentation](https://www.postgresql.org/support/versioning/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5984
msgid ""
"Support for Mattermost Server [Extended Support "
"Release](https://docs.mattermost.com/administration/extended-support-"
"release.html) (ESR) 5.19 has come to the end of its life cycle. Upgrading"
" to Mattermost Server v5.25 or later is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5985
msgid ""
"TLS versions 1.0 and 1.1 have been deprecated by browser vendors. "
"Starting in v5.31 (January 16, 2021) mmctl will return an error when "
"connected to Mattermost servers deployed with these TLS versions and "
"System Admins will need to explicitly add a flag in their commands to "
"continue to use them. We recommend upgrading to TLS version 1.2 or "
"higher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5988
msgid ""
"Now when the service crashes, it will generate a coredump instead of just"
" dumping the stack trace to the console. This allows us to preserve the "
"full information of the crash to help with debugging it. For more "
"information about coredumps, please see: https://man7.org/linux/man-"
"pages/man5/core.5.html."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5991
msgid ""
"If you upgrade from a release earlier than v5.27, please read the other "
"[Important Upgrade Notes](https://docs.mattermost.com/administration"
"/important-upgrade-notes.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5996
msgid ""
"New admin roles to delegate administration tasks to other types of "
"administrators (E20)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5997
msgid ""
"New admin roles are additional system roles that have access to "
"designated areas of the System Console. This enables you to delegate "
"certain administrative tasks to other members of your organization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:5999
msgid "Certificate-based authentication with AD/LDAP (E10)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6000
msgid ""
"You can now improve the security of your AD/LDAP authentication with "
"certificate-based AD/LDAP authentication."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6002
msgid "Stay current with in-product notices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6003
msgid ""
"With in-product notices, users and Admins will be made aware of the "
"newest product enhancements from within Mattermost. [Learn more about in-"
"product notices "
"here](https://docs.mattermost.com/administration/notices.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6008
msgid ""
"Improved the readability of the toast banner message timestamp, post "
"timestamp, and date separators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6009
msgid "Added animation for emoji reactions on webapp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6010
msgid ""
"Added the ability to use CTRL+B and CTRL+I to add bold and italics "
"markdown formatting to selected text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6011
msgid ""
"Clicking on original message creator's username in discontinuing posts "
"now opens the user's profile popover."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6012
msgid "Added support for PSD file preview."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6013
msgid ""
"When the **Enable Latex Rendering** option is set to ``true``, the "
"current code now doesn't highlight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6014
msgid "Updated the UX of the **More unreads** indicator in the channel sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6015
msgid ""
"**Select Team** list container now scales in width based on browser "
"window width."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6016
msgid ""
"Added support for signaling login to other tabs (Windows, macOS and Linux"
" browsers)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6018
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6264
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:6556
#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7422
