msgid ""
"Release v5.19 - [Extended Support "
"Release](https://docs.mattermost.com/administration/extended-support-"
"release.html)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7060
msgid ""
"Mattermost v5.19.0 contains low to high level security fixes. "
"[Upgrading](https://docs.mattermost.com/administration/upgrade.html) is "
"recommended. Details will be posted on our [security updates "
"page](https://mattermost.com/security-updates/) 30 days after release as "
"per the [Mattermost Responsible Disclosure Policy](https://mattermost.com"
"/security-vulnerability-report/?redirect_source=mm-org/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7062
msgid "**v5.19.3, released 2020-06-19**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7063
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue with the Plugin Tooltip implementation that caused links "
"to be truncated when rendered. This issue occured if you are using the "
"recent GitHub plugin v1.0.0 release. All links were affected, regardless "
"if they were related to GitHub. [MM-25808]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7064
msgid "**v5.19.2, released 2020-04-21**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7065
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue with unexpected crashes related to any action taken to "
"modify post properties such as push notifications. Note for developers: "
"Direct access to the ``Props`` field in the ``model.Post`` structure has "
"been deprecated. To avoid crash issues, the available ``GetProps()`` and "
"``SetProps()`` methods should now be used. Also, direct copy of the "
"``model.Post`` structure must be avoided in favor of the provided "
"``Clone()`` method. "
"[MM-21378](https://mattermost.atlassian.net/browse/MM-21378)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7066
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where a public channel appears in the list of Direct "
"Message channels in the channel sidebar if the channel name is 40 "
"characters long. "
