msgid "Removed and Deprecated Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7393
msgid ""
"Support for Internet Explorer (IE11) was removed. Learn more in our "
"[forum post](https://forum.mattermost.com/t/mattermost-is-dropping-"
"support-for-internet-explorer-ie11-in-v5-16/7575)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7396
msgid ""
"The Mattermost Desktop v4.3.0 release includes a change to how desktop "
"notifications are sent from non-secure URLs (http://). Organizations "
"using non-secure Mattermost Servers (http://) will need to update to "
"Mattermost Server versions 5.16.0+, 5.15.1, 5.14.4 or 5.9.5 (ESR) to "
"continue receiving desktop notifications when using Mattermost Desktop "
"v4.3.0 or later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7397
msgid ""
"When enabling [Guest Accounts](https://docs.mattermost.com/deployment"
"/guest-accounts.html), all users who have the ability to invite users "
"will be able to invite guests by default.  System admins will need to "
"remove this permission on each role via **System Console > Permissions "
"Schemes**.  In Mattermost Server version 5.17, the System admin will be "
"the only role to automatically get the invite guest permission, however "
"the fix will not be applicable in 5.16 due to database migration "
"processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7401
msgid "Guest Accounts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7402
msgid ""
"Provides a controlled and secure method for users outside of an "
"organization to collaborate with their organization without allowing the "
"guest to access proprietary or confidential information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7404
msgid "Plugin Marketplace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7405
msgid ""
"The integrations marketplace is built into the product and gives system "
"administrators the ability to discover and install Mattermost plugins "
"that are compatible with the server version you are running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7407
msgid "Improved user management"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/product-overview/unsupported-legacy-releases.md:7408
msgid ""
"System Administrators can view a user's team memberships and add a user "
"to additional teams from the System Console without having to be a member"
" of the team."
